* ''The focus test'' (operator, 2026-11-07: //"Pono, approve your leanss (talk them all out again n the open)."//, approving the house's lean: //does `M5` (page, CLI and MCP on one wiki) arrive sooner because of this? Where the answer reads "no, but it prevents a repeat," the item waits unless the repeat cost a real day//). Every new tools or process item meets this test before it opens. Measured against it: the broker's test door passes (every lane before the rite runs e2e through the controller's hands until it stands); the launcher's `P1-3` flake passes (two CI recurrences, each a full rerun); the pono lines on the remaining refusal messages wait.

